+# Backend
+
+Workflows backend: HogFlow models, services, providers and the facade other products reach it through
+
+## invariants
+- ses-only-through-provider: Only providers/ses.py imports boto3 or botocore; services reach AWS SES through the provider
+  over: every Python file under products/workflows/backend, apart from the paved path providers/ses.py, except the listed residual: test/test_ses_provider.py, test/test_ses_account_reputation_task.py
+  via: lint ruff:TID251 matching "ses-only-through-provider"
+  because: AWS/SES specifics (identity, region, retries) stay in the provider, so services use only the provider interface and never talk to AWS directly
+  refuted: staged services/_refute_ses_bypass.py importing boto3 and building an sesv2 client -> ruff TID251 went red at services/_refute_ses_bypass.py:1 naming ses-only-through-provider; clean again once removed (2026-09-30)
+  kinds: none
